### 3. Inconsistencies Identified

| # | Inconsistency | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | **Typo**: Root folder named `rullebook` — Architecture mandates `rulebook` | **Preserved** — renaming would break all existing documents that reference `rullebook/`. Document the discrepancy in manifest. |
| 2 | **Manifest says `tests/`** — Architecture Section 3 specifies `testing/` | **Used `testing/`** — Architecture is the single source of truth per hierarchy. |
| 3 | **Manifest references no `logs/` folder** — Architecture mandates it | **Created `logs/`** with 4 sub-directories. |

---

### 4. Improvements Made Beyond Raw Scaffolding

| Improvement | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Multi-stage Dockerfiles** | Smaller production images; separate build and runtime layers |
| **Non-root Docker users** | Security hardening per production best practices |
| **Docker health checks on every container** | Enables `depends_on: condition: service_healthy` |
| **Maven parent POM** | Single dependency version control for all 10 services |
| **Path aliases in tsconfig** (`@components/*`, etc.) | Clean imports throughout frontend |
| **PostgreSQL schemas** (not just tables) | Schema-per-domain isolation; future database-per-service migration is non-breaking |
| **Grafana + volume** added to docker-compose | Monitoring stack is complete from day one |
| **`.gitkeep` placeholders** | All directories are tracked by Git including empty ones |

